      "problem": "Find the right-sided limit at $x=32$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 32 \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{x}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {32}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Approaching from the right, we have $x>32,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt[5]{x}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {32}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {32}^{+}}\\sqrt[5]{x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[5]{32} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
